; sum four BCE unless declared training-loss hook\",\n      \"baseline\": \"Initial empirical reference: DIN local activation over item-field history with action values and four separate heads; field/task adaptation, not exact original DIN reproduction\",\n      \"research_goal\": \"Explore and validate mechanism-distinct unified modeling of multi-field user/context/target features and multi-feedback behavior histories. Develop representations and information flow that jointly support sequence modeling, feature interaction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\",\n      \"architecture_search\": {\n        \"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\",\n        \"design_dimensions\": [\n          \"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\",\n          \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\",\n          \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\",\n          \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\",\n          \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"\n        ],\n        \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\",\n        \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Select by the equal-weight validation AUC mean across click, cart, favorite and purchase; report macro Logloss and every task change. Use that same rule for checkpoints, parents, topic gains, merge eligibility and final selection. Evaluate mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost; compare closest architectural alternatives and the initial reference.\",\n        \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\",\n        \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspectable design references and nearest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"\n      },\n      \"research_budget\": {\n        \"seconds\": 43200,\n        \"start_event\": \"new_campaign_started_with_verified_dataset\",\n        \"start_unix\": 1794198624.5008233,\n        \"deadline_unix\": 1794241824.5008233\n      },\n      \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\",\n      \"source_sha256\": {\n        \"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\",\n        \"train.py\": \"a313f015c9d03ae8244861bc36ff58517d8b630b968c397f404f627ea631522e\",\n        \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\",\n        \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\",\n        \"selection.py\": \"aa519982aebe726806e1d11b68fca2574d33993778c3392997843fe489fd9aff\",\n        \"selection-policy.json\": \"8e568c065a0412009879a3d42569e3469df6e6b81fb2837f94a1e04d39ffacf4\"\n      },\n      \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n      \"benchmark_deviations\": [\n        \"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\",\n        \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\",\