{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /workspace/tools.py read paper:din --lines 65'","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n{\n  \"id\": \"paper:din\",\n  \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06978v4\",\n  \"version\": \"content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2\",\n  \"access_scope\": \"archived exact-version primary text; caching does not establish a local mechanism result\",\n  \"text_sha256\": \"83fb9eeca31e2fa3c557b6f08b893ad0018cefb33da6e00952136b9ce17e607e\",\n  \"total_lines\": 831,\n  \"start_line\": 1,\n  \"next_line\": 66,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"text\": \"1: Deep Interest Network for Click-Through Rate Prediction\\n2: Report GitHub Issue\\n3: ×\\n4: Title:\\n5: Content selection saved. Describe the issue below:\\n6: Description:\\n7: Submit without GitHub\\n8: Submit in GitHub\\n9: arXiv is now an independent nonprofit!\\n10: Learn more\\n11: ×\\n12: Back to arXiv\\n13: Why HTML?\\n14: Report Issue\\n15: Back to Abstract\\n16: Download PDF\\n17: Abstract.\\n18: 1 Introduction\\n19: 2 Relatedwork\\n20: 3 Background\\n21: 4 Deep Interest Network\\n22: 4.1 Feature Representation\\n23: 4.2 Base Model(Embedding&MLP)\\n24: Embedding layer\\n25: Pooling layer and Concat layer\\n26: MLP\\n27: Loss\\n28: 4.3 The structure of Deep Interest Network\\n29: 5 Training Techniques\\n30: 5.1 Mini-batch Aware Regularization\\n31: 5.2 Data Adaptive Activation Function\\n32: 6 Experiments\\n33: 6.1 Datasets and Experimental Setup\\n34: 6.2 Competitors\\n35: 6.3 Metrics\\n36: 6.4 Result from model comparison on Amazon Dataset and MovieLens Dataset\\n37: 6.5 Performance of regularization\\n38: 6.6 Result from model comparison on Alibaba Dataset\\n39: 6.7 Result from online A/B testing\\n40: 6.8 Visualization of DIN\\n41: 7 Conclusions\\n42: References\\n43: License: arXiv.org perpetual non-exclusive license\\n44: arXiv:1706.06978v4 [stat.ML] 13 Sep 2018\\n45: Deep Interest Network for Click-Through Rate Prediction\\n46: Conference: KDD’18; ; August 19–23, 2018, London, United Kingdom.CCS: Information systems Display advertisingCCS: Information systems Recommender systems\\n47: Guorui Zhou, Chengru Song, Xiaoqiang Zhu\\n48: Ying Fan, Han Zhu, Xiao Ma, Yanghui Yan, Junqi Jin, Han Li, Kun Gai\\n49: Affiliation: Alibaba Group\\n50: email: guorui.xgr, chengru.scr, xiaoqiang.zxq, zhuhan.zh, fanying.fy, maxiao.ma, yanghui.yyh, junqi.jjq, lihan.hl,jingshi.gk@alibaba-inc.com\\n51: © acmcopyright\\n52: Abstract.\\n53: Click-through rate prediction is an essential task in industrial applications, such as online advertising.\\n54: Recently deep learning based models have been proposed, which follow a similar Embedding&MLP paradigm.\\n55: In these methods large scale sparse input features are first mapped into low dimensional embedding vectors, and then transformed into fixed-length vectors in a group-wise manner, finally concatenated together to fed into a multilayer perceptron (MLP) to learn the nonlinear relations among features.\\n56: In this way, user features are compressed into a fixed-length representation vector, in regardless of what candidate ads are.\\n57: The use of fixed-length vector will be a bottleneck, which brings difficulty for Embedding&MLP methods to capture user’s diverse interests effectively from rich historical behaviors.\\n58: In this paper, we propose a novel model: Deep Interest Network (DIN) which tackles this challenge by designing a local activation unit to adaptively learn the representation of user interests from historical behaviors with respect to a certain ad.\\n59: This representation vector varies over different ads, improving the expressive ability of model greatly.\\n60: Besides, we develop two techniques: mini-batch aware regularization and data adaptive activation function which can help training industrial deep networks with hundreds of millions of parameters.\\n61: Experiments on two public datasets as well as an Alibaba real production dataset with over 2 billion samples demonstrate the effectiveness of proposed approaches, which achieve superior performance compared with state-of-the-art methods.\\n62: DIN now has been successfully deployed in the online display advertising system in Alibaba, serving the main traffic.\\n63: Keywords: Click-Through Rate Prediction, Display Advertising, E-commerce\\n64: 1. Introduction\\n65: In cost-per-click (CPC) advertising system, advertisements are ranked by the eCPM (effective cost per mille), which is the product of the bid price and CTR (click-through rate), and CTR needs to be predicted by the system. Hence, the performance of CTR prediction model has a direct impact on the final revenue and plays a key role in the advertising system. Modeling CTR prediction has received much attention from both research and industry community.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
